Publisher marks used for descriptive product and model identification

The Factory mark belongs to Factory. The OpenAI mark belongs to OpenAI.
The DeepSeek mark belongs to DeepSeek. The Meta mark belongs to Meta.
These marks are not Onyx branding and are not covered by an Onyx source-code
license. Their appearance does not imply sponsorship, endorsement, partnership,
or that an external product is installed or connected.

Original asset bytes are retained. Source URLs, ownership context, fingerprints
and the specific descriptive usage are recorded in app-sources.json.

Factory: https://factory.ai/ ; https://docs.factory.ai/
OpenAI: https://openai.com/brand/
DeepSeek: https://www.deepseek.com/ ; https://github.com/deepseek-ai
Meta Llama: https://github.com/meta-llama
Meta brand guidance: https://www.meta.com/brand/resources/meta/company-brand/

Codex CLI uses OpenAI's publisher identity beside the explicit Codex CLI name;
it is not a claim that the OpenAI mark is a separate Codex CLI product logo.
Droid uses Factory's official favicon beside the explicit Droid name. The
original factory.svg is retained unchanged. The displayed factory-qt.svg unwraps
its nested SVG and removes an unresolved clip reference for Qt compatibility;
all original shape geometry, colors and proportions are retained.
DeepSeek models use the official DeepSeek organization mark, separately from
the DeepSeek Harness application's own asset.
Llama models use the official Meta Llama organization mark beside their names.
